To convert markdown formatted text to HTML in C, you can use a third-party library like libMarkdown. Here's a sample function:

```cpp
#include <iostream>
#include <string>
#include <libMarkdown.h>

std::string markdownToHtml(const std::string& markdown) {
    markdown::Parser parser;
    markdown::Buffer input;
    markdown::Buffer output;

    // Parse the markdown text
    parser.parse(markdown, input);

    // Convert to HTML
    markdown::Html html;
    html.convert(input, output);

    return output.toString();
}

int main() {
    std::string markdown = "# Hello World\n\nThis is a sample.";
    std::string html = markdownToHtml(markdown);
    std::cout << "HTML: " << html << std::endl;
    return 0;
}
```

This function uses the libMarkdown library to convert markdown formatted text to HTML. The `Parser` object is used to parse the markdown text, and the `Html` object is used to convert it to HTML. The `Buffer` object is a temporary buffer used to store the input markdown and output HTML. Finally, the function returns the HTML formatted text as a string.

Note: You will need to install and link the libMarkdown library in your project to use this code.

